ance in task evidence; subsequent canonical preflights after landing must prove the real policy.\n\nRead repository instructions and the task class lifecycle. This is a small configuration change, not a Go behavior change: run JSON/parser and actual task-board preflight checks on candidate canonical config, including reviewer high not admitted and other providers excluded, plus repository-required local validation. No hosted CI, no synthetic status. Preserve every foreign board/index/worktree change. Use only task-board for board data. Leave the managed Story candidate UNCOMMITTED at its recorded checkpoint as the current merged checklist and handoff require; never make a producer commit on the Story branch. Task-board owns subsequent human-signed managed commits. Publish the correct derived Change Request and hand off ready for independent review. Primary owns Astra medium review and bound integration/PR/exact-head landing. Do not land or tag from this producer, do not spawn a reviewer or another producer.\n\nOnly the explicit config admission source changes for this bootstrap; do not create a reusable wrapper or patch task-board. The public tool documents and tests support external explicit config with unchanged project/runtime/control roots. Produce a concise outcome including candidate HEAD/tree, changed paths, command exits, policy observations and all limitations.\n\n\n\n### TASK-260909-3kvql5_approved-runtime-config.json\n{\n  \"mode\": \"local\",\n  \"local\": {\n    \"board_dir\": \".task-board\"\n  },\n  \"version_control\": {\n    \"confirm\": true,\n    \"desired_commit_time\": \"current real time; AX does not backdate commits\"\n  },\n  \"spawn\": {\n    \"enabled\": true,\n    \"max_parallel\": 20,\n    \"ceilings\": {\n      \"contract_version\": \"spawn-policy-v4\",\n      \"codex\": {\n        \"entries\": [\n          {\n            \"criterion\": \"equal\",\n            \"model\": \"gpt-6-astra\",\n            \"reasoning_effort\": \"medium\"\n   