n the worktree for the handoff to snapshot — never commit on the Story branch. A producer commit moves the branch tip off the recorded checkpoint and the handoff refuses with change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint; repair with `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\n- [ ] Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio — `n of m AC rows driven` — and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\n- [ ] Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\n- [ ] Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant — the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\n- [ ] A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\n- [ ] Lint clean\n- [ ] Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\n- [ ] New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\n- [ ] Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\n## Your Task\n\n- **ID**: TASK-260909-3kvql5\n- **Title**: TASK-260909-3kvql5: admit-muse-producers-and-medium-astra-reviewers\n- **Parent**: STORY-260909-2uobs6\n### Description\n\nApply the user-approved future model policy to canonical AX configuration: producers muse/muse-spark xhigh, reviewers codex/gpt-6-astra medium, existing active runs unchanged, orchestrators Codex Astra high or medium. Use only the authorized config delta and aligned documentation; preserve all product and delivery gates.\n### Scope\n\ntask-board.config.json and directly corresponding README model-policy documentation; task evidence.\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\nFresh canonical developer Muse xhigh and reviewer Astra medium preflights succeed; review role default and recommendations prefer medium; no unrelated runtime or hosted CI enabled; JSON and focused config checks pass; independent Astra medium review and signed exact-head PR landing complete.\n\n## Instructions\n\nThe following instructions have been attached to this task:\n\n### TASK-260909-3kvql5_producer-brief.md\n# Apply approved producer/reviewer routing\n\nUser explicitly changed future production to muse/muse-spark xhigh and future review to codex/gpt-6-astra medium. Existing runs may finish; orchestration remains Codex Astra high/medium. This is the bootstrap configuration task itself, launched through the supported explicit TASK_BOARD_CONFIG source because current canonical config is exclusive codex. The approved runtime config is an immutable operational input, not a published repository change. Do not alter it. Root runtime, control repository and board authority remain this AX repository.\n\nImplement the equivalent minimal model-policy delta in the managed Story worktree task-board.config.json. Use the approved-runtime-config.json as the requested policy reference, preserve all non-policy fields. Keep the mixed allow-set limited to Muse and Codex, existing unrelated dormant ceilings unchanged, Muse Spark xhigh admitted, reviewer role restricted/defaulted to Astra medium, review recommendations medium and producer workload recommendations Muse first. Leave architecture/orchestrator Astra choices usable. Align only the directly relevant README model-routing text; do not broaden product scope. Do not edit canonical root files or foreign worktrees. Record explicit-config bootstrap provenance in task evidence; subsequent canonical preflights after landing must prove the real policy.\n\nRead repository instructions and the task class lifecycle. This is a small configuration change, not a Go behavior change: run JSON/parser and actual task-board preflight checks on candidate canonical config, including reviewer high not admitted and other providers excluded, plus repository-required local validation. No hosted CI, no synthetic status. Preserve every foreign board/index/worktree change. Use only task-board for board data. Leave the managed Story candidate UNCOMMITTED at its recorded checkpoint as the current merged checklist and handoff require; never make a producer commit on the Story branch. Task-board owns subsequent human-signed managed commits. Publish the correct derived Change Request and hand off ready for independent review. Primary owns Astra medium review and bound integration/PR/exact-head landing. Do not land or tag from this producer, do not spawn a reviewer or another producer.\n\nOnly the explicit config admission source changes for this bootstrap; do not create a reusable wrapper or patch task-board. The public tool documents and tests support external explicit config with unchanged project/runtime/control roots. Produce a concise outcome including candidate HEAD/tree, changed paths, command exits, policy observations and all limitations.\n\n\n\n### TASK-260909-3kvql5_approved-runtime-config.json\n{\n  \"mode\": \"local\",\n  \"local\": {\n    \"board_dir\": \".task-board\"\n  },\n  \"version_control\": {\n    \"confirm\": true,\n    \"desired_commit_time\": \"current real time; AX does not backdate commits\"\n  },\n  \"spawn\": {\n    \"enabled\": true,\n    \"max_parallel\": 20,\n    \"ceilings\": {\n      \"contract_version\": \"spawn-policy-v4\",\n      \"codex\": {\n        \"entries\": [\n          {\n            \"criterion\": \"equal\",\n            \"model\": \"gpt-6-astra\",\n            \"reasoning_effort\": \"medium\"\n    