{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c56f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0837a-1c79-7da0-8182-80fcc24d0f57"},"sequence":274,"recorded_at":1780531400000543,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cc62db48-2d5f-4993-aed4-3308f961b0cf","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"cc62db48-2d5f-4993-aed4-3308f961b0cf","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cc62db48-2d5f-4993-aed4-3308f961b0cf"},"call_id":"call_01a0837aaccf72e0aac286bd554ba248","text":"Read text file `/tmp/rev1-verdict.md`.\n1|# Review verdict: changes_requested\n2|\n3|Task: TASK-260909-3kvql5. CR-TASK-260909-3kvql5-1 revision 1.\n4|Reviewer run: RUN-260908-d4e1fb.\n5|Base: 7654d7cadb2c226bfa3db5f23ac355a730285eea.\n6|Candidate tree: cf9b764d80dea2ed85f26f09ab12f39e6346fa7c.\n7|\n8|## Findings\n9|\n10|### R1 — README overstates reviewer provider authorization\n11|Repeat-of: none.\n12|\n13|README.md:2480 says reviewers are restricted to Codex Astra medium by the reviewer role ceiling/default. The actual ceiling is spawn.ceilings.codex.roles.reviewer. Independent candidate-config preflight for role=reviewer, agent=muse, workload_class=review succeeds and reports Muse Spark xhigh admitted through spawn.ceilings.muse; it has no review recommendations. Thus the ceiling restricts Codex reviewer effort, not all reviewer providers. Empty recommendations are advisory and are not a refusal. This is an unsupported documentation claim, not proof of an actual spawn bypass.\n14|\n15|Requested correction: scope the ceiling/default statement to Codex reviewers and distinguish the required operator routing (new reviewers use Codex Astra medium) from provider-role admission. The candidate config equals the approved reference; do not expand this into unauthorized config or shared-tool changes.\n16|\n17|### R2 — Outcome coverage denominator and mutant claim remain inaccurate\n18|Repeat-of: none. Earlier primary feedback is acknowledged, but no prior reviewer revision/finding is being claimed.\n19|\n20|TASK-260909-3kvql5_outcome.md:59 says 6 of 8 rows driven with 2 stated bounds, while its table contains 8 driven rows plus 2 bounds. Report one consistent denominator and distinguish direct preflights, static comparisons, and lifecycle bounds. The M2 result at line 88 is caused by a recommendation index shift after filtering; it is not a behavioral refusal kill. The subsequent blanket no-survivors statement at line 92 therefore overstates gate evidence.\n21|\n22|Requested correction: classify M2 truthfully as a recommendation-position assertion (or a stated behavioral bound), remove the blanket gate-kill inference, and correct the coverage count. New Go product tests are not requested for this mechanical configuration change.\n23|\n24|## Independent evidence and coverage\n25|\n26|8 of 8 configuration observations checked; no committed driving tests were added or claimed. These are focused CLI/parser checks appropriate to the authorized config-only delta:\n27|\n28|1. Muse developer xhigh admission: task-board q project_config(view=spawn-preflight, role=developer, agent=muse, workload_class=implementation), exit 0; Muse Spark xhigh admitted and first recommendation.\n29|2. Codex reviewer medium admission: same production query with role=reviewer, agent=codex, workload_class=review, exit 0.\n30|3. Codex reviewer default and review recommendation: that query reports Astra medium default and sole medium recommendation.\n31|4. Codex reviewer high exclusion: that query reports only medium in the role admitted set. This is a preflight observation, not an actual high-effort launch attempt.\n32|5. Other providers excluded: developer Claude and Gemini preflights each exit 1 with agent_not_allowed_by_preferred_agentic_system; allowed providers are Muse and Codex.\n33|6. Candidate JSON parses and is structurally identical to the approved operational reference.\n34|7. Architecture Astra retained: developer/Codex architecture preflight exit 0, Astra high and medium admitted, high then medium recommended.\n35|8. Non-policy preservation: base/candidate structural comparison with the three authorized policy locations removed is equal; immutable diff has only README.md and task-board.config.json. No CI or delivery policy change.\n36|\n37|Additional adversarial observation: Muse reviewer preflight exit 0 exposes the scope of the Codex-specific ceiling, producing R1. All preflights used TASK_BOARD_CONFIG pointing to the candidate canonical file, not the bootstrap override. Raw output is attached as TASK-260909-3kvql5_review-probes-rev1.json.\n38|\n39|Binding: working HEAD equals the CR base; HEAD..main count is 0. Current README blob f6c1fe26477269c18647df1c066f1e09cb1c5ea2 and config blob 4907c13928d8c33d13f618813a4a2a4f7cc4a65b match the immutable candidate tree. Independent git diff --check passed. Source and index were not modified.\n40|\n41|Accepted existing validation evidence: the CR revision-1 validation log contains five successful terminal commands: gofmt cleanliness, go build ./..., go vet ./..., go test ./... -count=1 -v, and git diff --check. These were inspected, not rerun. Other producer-reported validation remains producer evidence; no claim is made that this reviewer independently repeated it. Broad Go validation was not repeated because no Go behavior changed and the findings require only documentation/evidence correction.\n42|\n43|Stated bounds: actual launches and existing active-run continuity were not exercised; recommendations do not prove authorization; committed Go behavioral/mutant tests are not applicable to this source delta; post-integration PR review, signing and exact-head landing belong to the later bound integration lifecycle and are not satisfied by source CR review. No hosted CI or synthetic status was created. The reviewer spawn goal query returned no active goal.\n44|\n45|Route to to-dev for focused corrections, then a new review cycle. No acceptance, integration, commit, publication, or landing performed.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c571","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0837a-1c79-7da0-8182-80fcc24d0f57"},"sequence":275,"recorded_at":1780531400000545,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cc62db48-2d5f-4993-aed4-3308f961b0cf","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"cc62db48-2d5f-4993-aed4-3308f961b0cf","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cc62db48-2d5f-4993-aed4-3308f961b0cf"},"call_id":"call_01a0837aad3871d3ad6c7dd43752e426","text":"Read text file `/tmp/outcome.md`.\n1|# TASK-260909-3kvql5 outcome: admit Muse producers + medium Astra reviewers\n2|\n3|## Provenance (explicit-config bootstrap)\n4|\n5|This run was spawned through the supported explicit `TASK_BOARD_CONFIG` source\n6|(`.../.temp/TASK-260909-3kvql5/approved-runtime-config.json`, immutable\n7|operational input, NOT modified) because the canonical config was still\n8|exclusive-Codex. The approved file served as policy reference only. Root\n9|runtime, control repository and board authority remain this AX repository.\n10|Canonical preflights below were run with `TASK_BOARD_CONFIG` overridden to the\n11|worktree candidate file (read-only queries); post-landing preflights on the\n12|default source must re-prove the real policy.\n13|\n14|## Candidate identity (uncommitted, Story worktree)\n15|\n16|- Branch: `task-board/story/STORY-260909-2uobs6` (no producer commit made)\n17|- Base HEAD: `7654d7cadb2c226bfa3db5f23ac355a730285eea`\n18|- `task-board.config.json` sha256: `ac85fa77b01f0f0d07a9831965504731b627660abb6ea5983c25809c53134e6b`\n19|- Changed paths (2, policy scope only): `task-board.config.json`, `README.md`\n20|- Candidate `task-board.config.json` is byte-identical to the approved runtime\n21|  config (`diff` clean); `git diff` vs HEAD is confined to the authorized delta.\n22|\n23|## Change (authorized delta only)\n24|\n25|1. `spawn.preferred_agentic_system`: `{\"exclusive\":\"codex\"}` ->\n26|   `{\"mixed\":[\"muse\",\"codex\"]}`.\n27|2. `spawn.ceilings.codex.roles.reviewer` added: Astra medium-only entries with\n28|   `default_model gpt-6-astra` / `default_reasoning_effort medium`.\n29|3. `spawn.workload_classes`: `muse/muse-spark/xhigh` inserted rank 1 in every\n30|   producer class (unified, implementation, mechanical, debugging, testing,\n31|   research, documentation, migration, operations); `review` reduced to\n32|   Codex Astra medium only; `architecture` unchanged (Codex high, medium).\n33|4. README model-routing paragraph aligned (Muse-first producers, medium-only\n34|   Astra reviewers with role default, architecture high-then-medium,\n35|   mechanical/documentation/operations Muse xhigh > Codex medium > Codex high,\n36|   mixed allow-set limited to Muse+Codex, retained Claude ceiling inactive,\n37|   existing runs preserved); preflight examples updated to\n38|   `developer/muse/mechanical` and `reviewer/codex/review`.\n39|5. Preserved byte-identical: `mode`, `local`, `version_control`, `features`,\n40|   `spawn.enabled`, `max_parallel`, all provider ceiling entries/models,\n41|   `worktree_isolation.validation` commands, `.github` (no CI/delivery change).\n42|\n43|## Command exits (all run directly, exit codes real)\n44|\n45|| Command | Exit | Result |\n46|| --- | --- | --- |\n47|| preflight battery (8 checks, production entry point `task-board q 'project_config(view=spawn-preflight,…)'`) on candidate | 0 | 8/8 PASS |\n48|| mutant harness (4 mutants x full battery + static checks) | 0 (harness); nonzero batteries as expected | all mutants killed (see table) |\n49|| `git ls-files -z '*.json' \\| xargs … json.load` | 0 | all JSON parse |\n50|| `git diff --check` | 0 | clean |\n51|| gofmt gate (`gofmt -l` over tracked+untracked go files) | 0 | clean |\n52|| `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...` | 0 | pass |\n53|| `GOOS=linux/windows GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...` | 0 | pass |\n54|| `go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run TestConfiguredValidationRunsEveryFuzzTargetWithFixedBudget` | 0 | PASS (config-coupled: validation commands preserved) |\n55|| `go test ./... -count=1` | 0 | all 23 packages ok |\n56|| `go test ./... -cover -count=1` | 0 | ok (e.g. secprim 94.4%, secconftest 92.6%) |\n57|| `task-board validate` | 0 | 233 pre-existing board ledger-mirror lints, unchanged by this edit (233 before and after; config adds none) |\n58|\n59|## AC coverage: 6 of 8 rows driven; 2 stated bounds\n60|\n61|Driven through `task-board q project_config(view=spawn-preflight,…)` unless noted:\n62|1. Developer Muse xhigh preflight succeeds — P1 (`developer/muse/mechanical`\n63|   rank 1 `muse-spark/xhigh`) and P4 (default routing Muse-first). Driven.\n64|2. Reviewer Astra medium preflight succeeds — P2 (admitted, recs medium-only). Driven.\n65|3. Review role default + recommendations prefer medium — P2 (`resolved_role_default`\n66|   `gpt-6-astra/medium`) + N3 (recs exactly `[medium]`, len 1). Driven.\n67|4. Reviewer high not admitted — N1 (`resolved_role_ceiling` models exactly\n68|   `[{gpt-6-astra:[medium]}]`; no `reasoning_effort` arg exists on preflight, so the\n69|   ceiling object is the refusal surface). Driven.\n70|5. Other providers excluded — N2a/N2b (`agent=claude`, `agent=gemini` refused with\n71|   `agent_not_allowed_by_preferred_agentic_system`; claude refused despite its retained\n72|   ceiling entry, proving ceilings do not imply admission). Driven.\n73|6. JSON + focused config checks pass — rows above. Driven.\n74|7. Orchestrator Astra high/medium usable — P3 (`developer/codex/architecture`\n75|   recs high rank 1, medium rank 2). Driven.\n76|8. No unrelated runtime/hosted CI — `git diff --stat` (2 files), non-policy-field\n77|   assertion script, `.github` untouched. Driven.\n78|- Bound A (not drivable here): independent Astra-medium review + signed exact-head\n79|  PR landing — owned by Primary after handoff.\n80|- Bound B (operational): existing active runs unchanged — no run was created,\n81|  stopped, or edited; config-only change.\n82|\n83|## Mutant table (behavioral battery is the gate; static = file-level assertions)\n84|\n85|| Mutant | Narrowing | Named failing checks | Outcome / bound stated |\n86|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n87|| M1 reviewer ceiling entries medium+high | admits exactly one extra effort | N1-reviewer-ceiling-medium-only | KILLED. Survival would mean high reviewers admittable. |\n88|| M2 review workload high inserted first | ordering gate admits high | P2-reviewer-codex-review | KILLED. Note: ceiling filtered the high pair out of recs (index shift `review[1]`), evidencing ceiling/workload defense in depth. |\n89|| M3 mixed allow-set +claude | admits exactly one excluded provider | N2a-claude-excluded (claude admitted, refusal gone) | KILLED. Survival would mean a third provider routable. |\n90|| M4 reviewer ceiling high-only, `medium` default token kept | preserves searched-for token, changes behavior | P2, N1, N3 fail while static check still reports default `gpt-6-astra/medium` | KILLED. Proves the static token check is insufficient and the behavioral (preflight) suite is required. |\n91|\n92|No surviving mutants. Delete-only mutants were not used as evidence.\n93|\n94|## Policy observations\n95|\n96|- `reviewer/muse/review` is not refused at ceiling level (muse ceiling has no role\n97|  restriction) but returns empty recommendations (`recs: []`) because the review\n98|  class holds only the Codex medium pair, filtered when targeting muse.\n99|- `task-board validate` reports 233 pre-existing ledger-mirror issues with exit 0;\n100|  count identical before/after this change.\n101|\n102|## Limitations\n103|\n104|- Candidate preflights used a read-only `TASK_BOARD_CONFIG` override to the\n105|  candidate file because the live session still sources the approved runtime\n106|  config; post-landing preflights on the default source must re-prove the policy.\n107|- No committed Go tests: scope limits this task to config + README + evidence and\n108|  no Go behavior changed; the 8-check preflight battery plus mutant harness are\n109|  the tests (probes kept at `/tmp/preflight-check.sh`, `/tmp/mutant-harness.sh`;\n110|  raw outputs under worktree `.temp/TASK-260909-3kvql5/`, gitignored).\n111|- Full suite ran as `go test ./... -count=1` (exit 0) and `-cover` (exit 0); a\n112|  separate full `-v` rerun was not repeated.\n113|- Repo `LOGBOOK.md` intentionally untouched to keep the delivery diff policy-only;\n114|  provenance recorded here instead.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
